---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/pages/services.css';
---

<Layout title="The Operation: SecureProspective" description="Insurance producer infrastructure is SecureProspective's revenue-producing operating foundation.">
  <Nav />

  <main id="main" class="operation-page" transition:name="page-card">
    <section class="operation-hero" aria-labelledby="operation-title" data-operation-hero>
      <div class="operation-hero-grid shell">
        <aside class="operation-rail" aria-label="Operation page index">
          <div class="operation-rail-top">
            <span class="operation-rail-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>FILE // 001</span>
          </div>
          <p class="operation-rail-name">THE OPERATION</p>
          <div class="operation-rail-status">
            <span>STATUS</span>
            <strong>ACTIVE</strong>
          </div>
          <nav class="operation-index" aria-label="On this page">
            <a href="#operating-record" aria-current="location"><span>01</span><span>Record</span></a>
            <a href="#producer-work"><span>02</span><span>Work now</span></a>
            <a href="#sp-plus-consequence"><span>03</span><span>Consequence</span></a>
            <a href="#conversation"><span>04</span><span>Conversation</span></a>
          </nav>
        </aside>

        <div class="operation-hero-body">
          <div class="operation-heading">
            <h1 id="operation-title">The operation is not a footnote.</h1>
            <p>
              SecureProspective serves producers now. The IMO is the revenue engine, the field environment,
              and the source of every constraint the prospective system must answer.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="operation-evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
            <div class="operation-evidence-head">
              <span id="evidence-title">Operating figures</span>
              <span>Approximate / current record</span>
            </div>
            <table class="operation-facts">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">SecureProspective operating figures</caption>
              <tbody>
                <tr data-proof-row>
                  <th scope="row">Active producers</th>
                  <td>Approximately <strong>8</strong></td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-proof-row>
                  <th scope="row">Annual annuity volume assisted</th>
                  <td>Approximately <strong>$18M</strong> current</td>
                </tr>
                <tr data-proof-row>
                  <th scope="row">Production assisted</th>
                  <td>Approximately <strong>$110M</strong> across six years</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <div class="operation-evidence-note">
              <span>Operating posture</span>
              <strong>Active, revenue-producing, accountable to real cases.</strong>
            </div>
          </div>

          <a class="operation-hero-link" href="#operating-record">
            Read the operating record <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="operating-record" class="operation-panel operation-panel--blue" data-deal aria-labelledby="record-title">
      <div class="operation-panel-grid shell">
        <aside class="operation-panel-marker">
          <strong>01</strong>
          <span>Operating record</span>
        </aside>
        <div class="operation-panel-body">
          <div class="operation-intro">
            <h2 id="record-title">Insurance producer infrastructure.</h2>
            <p>
              Independent financial professionals and small IMOs need more than product access. They need
              case intelligence, suitability discipline, carrier positioning, and an operating structure that
              can carry responsibility from first conversation through issue.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="operation-test">
            <span>Operational test</span>
            <strong>Can the structure carry responsibility from first conversation through issue?</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="producer-work" class="operation-panel operation-panel--white" data-deal aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="operation-panel-grid shell">
        <aside class="operation-panel-marker">
          <strong>02</strong>
          <span>What we do now</span>
        </aside>
        <div class="operation-panel-body">
          <h2 id="work-title">The work producers can use today.</h2>
          <ol class="operation-worklist">
            <li>
              <span class="operation-work-label">CASE // 01</span>
              <strong>Advanced case design</strong>
              <p>Structure complex client situations before a product is allowed to become the answer.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="operation-work-label">POSITION // 02</span>
              <strong>Carrier and product positioning</strong>
              <p>Fit the solution to the full client picture, not to a shelf or a sales target.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="operation-work-label">FEDERAL // 03</span>
              <strong>Federal benefits specialty</strong>
              <p>FERS, CSRS, TSP, FEHB, and LEO, ATC, and researcher variations.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="operation-work-label">CONTROL // 04</span>
              <strong>Suitability and best interest</strong>
              <p>Annuity suitability workflows and NY Regulation 187 discipline built into the case process.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="operation-work-label">FIELD // 05</span>
              <strong>Producer development</strong>
              <p>Training and operating support for agents who intend to build durable production.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="operation-work-label">SYSTEM // 06</span>
              <strong>IMO infrastructure</strong>
              <p>The connective operating work between producer, client, carrier, case, and obligation.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <a class="operation-inline-action" href="mailto:secureprospective@gmail.com?subject=Producer%20infrastructure%20conversation">
            Start a producer conversation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="sp-plus-consequence" class="operation-panel operation-panel--silver" data-deal aria-labelledby="consequence-title">
      <div class="operation-panel-grid shell">
        <aside class="operation-panel-marker">
          <strong>03</strong>
          <span>Why it matters</span>
        </aside>
        <div class="operation-panel-body">
          <div class="operation-intro operation-intro--single">
            <h2 id="consequence-title">This operation gives SP+ consequences.</h2>
            <p>
              SP+ answers a problem visible inside the operation: advisors handling client PII, annuities, and
              retirement assets on general-purpose home computers. The first deliverable is an immutable Fedora
              workstation with full-disk encryption, practical application containment, and the Pi AI harness
              integrated into the daily desktop.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="operation-bridge" aria-label="The operating foundation leads to the first deliverable">
            <span>Current operation</span>
            <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <strong>SP+</strong>
            <span>First deliverable</span>
          </div>

          <dl class="operation-state-table">
            <div>
              <dt>Foundation</dt>
              <dd>Immutable Fedora</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Protection</dt>
              <dd>Encrypted and contained</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Workflow</dt>
              <dd>Human-held AI</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
          <a class="operation-text-link" href="/the-work#sp-plus">See what is being built from it <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="conversation" class="operation-panel operation-panel--ink" data-deal aria-labelledby="conversation-title">
      <div class="operation-panel-grid shell">
        <aside class="operation-panel-marker">
          <strong>04</strong>
          <span>Current invitation</span>
        </aside>
        <div class="operation-panel-body operation-invitation">
          <h2 id="conversation-title">If the work is insurance, start here.</h2>
          <p>Bring the case, the producer constraint, or the infrastructure problem. The first move is a direct conversation about what is actually happening.</p>
          <a class="operation-cta" href="/contact">Choose the conversation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../scripts/motion.js';
  import '../scripts/pages/services.js';
</script>
